        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: рассчитывать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "рассчитывать (rasschítyvat) — \"to count on, to rely on; to calculate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Мы рассчитываем на твою помощь. My rasschítyvayem na tvoyú pómoshch. We are counting on your help."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective рассчитать (to calculate). Рассчитывать на + accusative — to count on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "рассчитывать (rasschítyvat) is built from рас- and считать \"to count\", on the root of число \"number\", Proto-Slavic čislo (EtymDB). To count on someone was first to reckon them in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
